atched counties: 3108\n- Unmatched boundary counties: 0\n\nNotes:\n- The population table contains 113 GEOIDs not present in the contiguous boundary layer. These are expected to be outside the contiguous U.S. set or otherwise excluded from that boundary file.\n\nOutputs:\n- Final GeoDataFrame registered as: `contiguous_counties_population_2021_joined`\n- GeoJSON written to:\n  `/home/abk6234/GAS/mysite2/Data/contiguous_counties_population_2021_joined.geojson`\n\nKey output field:\n- `population_2021` → numeric (`int64`) and ready for quantile classification later.", "dataset_path": "Data/county_join_759877_276576.geojson"}, "duration": "33.69s", "script": "import pandas as pd\nimport geopandas as gpd\n\n# File paths\ncounties_path = \"Data/contiguous_counties_863529_701650.geojson\"\npopulation_path = \"/home/abk6234/GAS/mysite2/Data/tabular_2021_418675.csv\"\nout_path = \"/home/abk6234/GAS/mysite2/Data/contiguous_counties_population_2021_joined.geojson\"\n\n# Load data once\ncounties = gpd.read_file(counties_path)\npop = pd.read_csv(population_path)\n\n# Keep only 2021 records if a year column exists\nif \"year\" in pop.columns:\n    pop = pop.loc[pop[\"year\"] == 2021].copy()\n\n# Construct standard 5-digit county GEOID from state and county codes\npop[\"GEOID\"] = (\n    pd.to_numeric(pop[\"state_fips\"], errors=\"coerce\").astype(\"Int64\").astype(str).str.zfill(2)\n    + pd.to_numeric(pop[\"county_fips\"], errors=\"coerce\").astype(\"Int64\").astype(str).str.zfill(3)\n)\n\n# Ensure population is numeric for later quantile classification\npop[\"population_2021\"] = pd.to_numeric(pop[\"B01001_001E:Total:\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n\n# Check for duplicate GEOIDs in the population table\ndup_count = int(pop[\"GEOID\"].duplicated().sum())\nprint(\"Duplicate GEOIDs in population table:\", dup_count)\nif dup_count:\n    dup_cols = [c for c in [\"GEOID\", \"state_fips\", \"county_fips\", \"year\"] if c in pop.columns]\n    print(pop.loc[pop[\"GEOID\"].duplicated(keep=False), dup_cols].sort_values(\"GEOID\").head(20))\n\n# Join population to contiguous county boundaries\njoin_cols = [c for c in [\"GEOID\", \"population_2021\", \"B01001_001E:Total:\", \"state_fips\", \"county_fips\", \"year\", \"source\"] if c in pop.columns]\nresult = counties.merge(pop[join_cols], on=\"GEOID\", how=\"left\", validate=\"1:1\")\n\n# Verify join coverage\nmatched = int(result[\"population_2021\"].notna().sum())\nunmatched = int(result[\"population_2021\"].isna().sum())\nprint(\"Boundary counties:\", len(result))\nprint(\"Matched counties:\", matched)\nprint(\"Unmatched counties:\", unmatched)\n\nif unmatched:\n    unmatched_cols = [c for c in [\"GEOID\", \"STATEFP\", \"COUNTYFP\", \"NAME\", \"STUSPS\", \"STATE_NAME\"] if c in result.columns]\n    unmatched_df = result.loc[result[\"population_2021\"].isna(), unmatched_cols].copy()\n    print(\"Unmatched county examples:\")\n    print(unmatched_df.head(20))\nelse:\n    print(\"Join coverage is complete for contiguous counties.\")\n\n# Check for population-table counties not present in the contiguous boundary layer\nextra_tabular = sorted(set(pop[\"GEOID\"]) - set(counties[\"GEOID\"]))\nprint(\"Population table GEOIDs not in contiguous boundary layer:\", len(extra_tabular))\nif extra_tabular:\n    extra_cols = [c for c in [\"GEOID\", \"state_fips\", \"county_fips\", \"population_2021\", \"year\", \"source\"] if c in pop.columns]\n    print(pop.loc[pop[\"GEOID\"].isin(extra_tabular), extra_cols].head(20))\n\n# Confirm numeric dtype\nprint(result[[\"GEOID\", \"population_2021\"]].dtypes)\n\n# Write output\nresult.to_file(out_path, driver=\"GeoJSON\")\nprint(\"Wrote GeoJSON to:\", out_path)", "metrics": {"llm_calls": 4, "tool_calls": 2, "number of artifacts": 1}}}, {"step": 5, "agent": "MapProjectionAgent", "instruction": "Reproject the joined county dataset to a Lambert Conformal Conic coordinate reference system.", "dataset_from_steps": [4], "dataset_aliases": {}, "result": {"agent_name": "MapProjectionAgent", "agent_version": "2.0.0", "model": "gpt-4o", "duration": "7.97s", "total_input_tokens": 2693, "total_output_tokens": 266, "inputs": {"text": "Reproject the joined county dataset to a Lambert Conformal Conic coordinate reference system.", "dataset_path": "Data/county_join_759877_276576.geojson"}, "outputs": {"text": "The county dataset has been successfully reprojected to the 'USA Contiguous Lambert Conformal Conic' coordinate reference system (ESRI:102004). This CRS is specifically tailored for the contiguous United States, ensuring accurate area and distance measurements, which is ideal for regional analysis at the county level. The Lambert Conformal Conic projection minimizes distortion for east-west oriented areas, making it a perfect fit for your dataset.\n\nTechnical Report:\nThe 'USA Contiguous Lambert Conformal Conic' (ESRI:102004) is selected as the most appropriate CRS for the task of reprojecting a county dataset within the United States. This CRS is specifically designed for the contiguous United States (CONUS) and is ideal for regional analysis, preserving area and shape across large extents. The Lambert Conformal Conic projection is well-suited for mid-latitude countries like the USA, providing minimal distortion for east-west extents, which is typical for county-level datasets. This choice ensures accurate representation and measurement of distances and areas within the dataset, making it superior to global CRSs for this specific regional application.", "dataset_path": "/home/abk6234/GAS/mysite2/Output/Reproject_the_joined_county_dataset_to_a_034967.geojson", "dataset_size": {"type": "GeoDataFrame", "dimensions": null, "feature_count": 3108}}, "metrics": {"llm_calls": 3, "tool_calls": 2, "number of artifacts": 1}, "environment": {"python_version": "3.12.13", "domain-specific libraries": ["pandas", "geopandas", "pyproj", "requests", "openai"]}, "script": null, "additional": {"Execution": {"Inputs": {"text_query": "Reproject the joined county datase